reason = 0.66b2 declares wrapt ~= 1.0, which is the only term in the injected
    tree that rejects wrapt 2.x, and one rejected line stands the whole
    distribution down. open-telemetry/opentelemetry-python-contrib#5117 widened
    the requirement to wrapt >= 1.0.0, < 3.0.0 on 2026-10-01, after the 0.66
    patch branch had split, so no 0.66 release carries it. The source here is
    the v0.66b2 source verbatim; only the requirement changes.
removal = Every step, because none of them fails on its own if it is missed and
    the wheel-contents step fails CI if it is not taken. Delete this directory.
    Restore opentelemetry-instrumentation-asyncclick to [project].dependencies
    of packages/dash0-opentelemetry/pyproject.toml, and drop from that file the
    [project.optional-dependencies] instruments table, the asyncclick entry
    under [project.entry-points.opentelemetry_instrumentor], and the asyncclick
    and anyio entries of the dev dependency group. Drop the three asyncclick
    paths from the wheel-contents step of .github/workflows/ci.yml, the
    asyncclick exclusion from ruff.toml, the asyncclick entry of
    EXEMPT_FROM_EXACT_PIN in scripts/check_pinned_dependencies.py and its tests,
    the dash0-opentelemetry key of upstream_packages_shadowed_by_shipped_packages
    in sitecustomize.py and its entry in the shadowed list of
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_sitecustomize.py, and the
    VENDORED_INSTRUMENTATIONS entry in
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_instrumentations.py. Delete
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_vendored_asyncclick.py. Drop the
    asyncclick paragraph from docs/auto-instrumentation.md, the asyncclick row
    and the paragraph under it from docs/kubernetes-injection.md, the asyncclick
    deviation bullet from packages/dash0-opentelemetry/README.rst, and the
    second derivation command and the asyncclick sentence of the project
    overview from the root CLAUDE.md. Then run uv lock, which the uv lock
    --check job requires, and regenerate all-dependencies.txt.
